# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not, so never put
# a real token here.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# Only scripts/analytics.mjs reads these. The site build takes SITE_URL from the
# Worker's build variables in Cloudflare, not from here.

# dash.cloudflare.com > My Profile > API Tokens > Create Token > Custom Token.
# Exactly two permissions, both read-only, and they are enough:
#
#   Account : Account Analytics : Read     the Web Analytics beacon
#   Zone    : Analytics         : Read     raw User-Agents at the edge
#
# The script also tries to read the beacon's own configuration for its header
# line. That sits behind a broader account permission, and a token with only
# the two above cannot do it. The script says so and carries on — the counts
# never depend on it, so there is no reason to widen the token for it.
#
# The token `wrangler login` caches will not work here — its scopes cover
# Workers deploys, not analytics.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Right-hand sidebar of the account home page, or `npx wrangler whoami`.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=

# Overview page of the asacerdotiza.com.br zone, under "Zone ID".
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=

# Web Analytics > the site > the beacon snippet. It is the value the snippet
# labels `token`, and it is not a secret — it ships in the page's HTML.
CLOUDFLARE_RUM_SITE=
